Testing [16. Face Workflow]: "can faculty register faces?"
Reply: Faculty members do not have a built‑in capability to register facial data in EduManager. Attendance for faculty‑managed courses is handled via manual check‑ins or live QR attendance sessions, but the platform doesn’t support face‑registration for those courses. If you need facial recognition for attendance, that functionality is currently reserved for the system’s automated face‑attendance modules, which are available to administrators and the core system, not to individual faculty accounts.

Testing [16. Face Workflow]: "can student register their own face?"
Reply: In the current EduManager system, face data for attendance is **not** something a student can upload or register themselves. Face registration is handled by the system administrators or the faculty team when they set up attendance sessions. If you need a face‑based attendance method for a class, please contact an Admin or the faculty member in charge of that course, and they can enable or configure the face‑recognition feature for you.

